MHCLG RED - RED National Situation Report No. 4
As at 1400, Thursday 15 January 2026

Handling: OFFICIAL. Not for onward distribution outside government and LRF pa=
rtners.

A. Storm Fenella
Status: Major incident declared. Response phase.
Lead: the Cumbria LRF and Lancashire LRF
Key points:
  - Fellside Care Home: EVACUATED (run by Fellside Care Ltd)
  - Pooley Bridge crossing: CLOSED
  - Keswick School: open as rest centre
  - A591 near Thirlmere: remains closed (flooding)

B. Penrith boil water incident
Status: Active response
Lead: Cumbria LRF
Key points:
  - Penrith Leisure Centre: OPEN for collection (run by United Utilities)
  - Eamont Moor Water Treatment Works: out of service
  - Castle Park: bottled water station open

C. Central government
RED duty officer in contact with the LRF secretariats. Next report at 0800 to=
morrow.

Regards,
Sian Pryce
Resilience Adviser, RED, MHCLG

